N5008 [temp.inst]/11, [dcl.spec.auto.general]/12, [class.mem.general]/8:
view_interface<ref_view<int>>::front() has a deduced return type and is
never used, so its definition is not instantiated; ref_view<int> is
complete where __member_begin<ref_view<int> &> is evaluated, and its
member `begin' satisfies the requirement. The front end instantiated
front()'s body while view_interface<ref_view<int>> -- ref_view's base --
is being instantiated, i.e. before ref_view<int> has its members; the body
evaluated the constraint of ranges::begin, __member_begin<ref_view<int> &>
came out false and was kept, so the later use was false as well. Members
with a deduced return type of class template specializations are now
deferred like any other member and converted when a call needs their type.
cvise reduction (/tmp/r163/red/nf_mb) of libstdc++'s <ranges>, where the
parser's compound-requirement fast path (parse.cpp "Try compound
requirement") happened to hide it: without the fast path
cpp20_ranges_basic drops ranges_util.h:84 and operator| (round 163i). g++
13 and clang++ 18 accept the program. Fails on bin53.
